keiki_mcp.description:
Revoke a purchase: cancels its payment credential so it can no longer be charged, and returns the updated purchase. Owners and admins only.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

DELETE /agents/:id/wallet/intents/:intentId → { status, ok, data, error }

Disconnect payments; returns { ok }. Owners/admins only.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

DELETE /payments → { status, ok, data, error }

Delete a payee; returns { ok }. Owners/admins only.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

DELETE /payments/payees/:id → { status, ok, data, error }

Buy usage credits for the organization; owners and admins only. Charges the saved payment method, or returns a checkoutUrl to share with the user when none is saved; a null URL means the credits were added.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

POST /billing/credits/purchase → { status, ok, data, error }

Buy a voice number in the area code or state (or any US number when neither is given) and connect it to the agent for inbound phone calls (charges the org). Returns the identity id and the purchased number. With `forwardFrom`, the agent's iMessage line forwards its calls to a hidden voice number instead and stays the public number; `forwarding` is `active`, or `pending` while the line's provider sets it up.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

POST /identities/phone-calls → { status, ok, data, error }

Buy a new iMessage line for the organization from Photon (default) or Blooio, optionally with a coupon and connected straight to an agent. Owners and admins only. Returns a `checkoutUrl` the user must open when payment details are needed. Otherwise the selected provider provisions the line; when `DEFAULT_IMESSAGE_PROVIDER` is set, it overrides the request body’s `provider`. A Photon line is provisioned immediately and its `phoneNumber` returned; a Blooio purchase may instead return `status: "provisioning"` (or `"action_required"` with an `actionUrl`) and a `requestId` to follow with GET /lines/provisioning/:id.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

POST /lines/purchase → { status, ok, data, error }

Make another member the owner of the organization; the current owner becomes an admin. Owner only. Find the member’s user id with the member list first.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

POST /members/transfer-ownership → { status, ok, data, error }

Start payment identity verification; returns { url }. Owners/admins only.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

POST /payments/identity-verification → { status, ok, data, error }

Connect Grosso using { apiKey }; returns { account } without its key. Owners/admins only.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

POST /payments/key → { status, ok, data, error }

Switch payments to live mode; returns { account }. Owners/admins only.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

POST /payments/live → { status, ok, data, error }

Create { ownerEmail, agentId, maxAmount, dailyAmount } (integer cents); returns { payee, onboardingUrl }. Owners/admins only.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

POST /payments/payees → { status, ok, data, error }

Assign a payee with { agentId }; returns { payee }. Owners/admins only.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

POST /payments/payees/:id → { status, ok, data, error }

Start Grosso signup with { email, name }; returns { account }. Owners/admins only.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

POST /payments/signup → { status, ok, data, error }

Verify signup with { code, acceptTerms: true }; returns { account }. Owners/admins only.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

POST /payments/verify → { status, ok, data, error }

Turn auto top-up on or off; owners and admins only. While enabled, credits are bought with the saved payment method whenever the balance falls below threshold. threshold and quantity are required even when disabling.

Destructive — deleting, spending money, or changing who has access. Show the user what it will do and get their confirmation first.

PUT /billing/auto-top-up → { status, ok, data, error }
